the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
*a claim* is covered.
*a claim* is under the buildings section.
*a claim* is under the contents section.
*a claim* concerns damage to the structure.
*a claim* concerns gradual wear.
*a claim* concerns *an item*.
*an item* is a household item.

the knowledge base claims includes:

a claim is covered
    if the claim is under the buildings section
    or the claim is under the contents section.

a claim is under the buildings section
    if the claim concerns damage to the structure
    and it is not the case that
        the claim concerns gradual wear.

a claim is under the contents section
    if the claim concerns an item
    and the item is a household item.

tv is a household item.

scenario pipe is:
    c1 concerns damage to the structure.
    covered expects answers ["c1 is covered"].

scenario wear is:
    c2 concerns damage to the structure.
    c2 concerns gradual wear.
    covered expects answers [].

scenario tv is:
    c3 concerns tv.
    covered expects answers ["c3 is covered"].

query covered is:
    which claim is covered.
